     <actual value="1">
      <location ref="Africa"></location>
      <dimension name="Gender" value="Female"></dimension>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1 policy advocacy initiative was undertaken, resulting in the submission of written demands to the Mombasa County Assembly aimed at influencing GBV-related policy reform.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1">
      <location ref="Africa"></location>
      <dimension name="Gender" value="Female"></dimension>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The reporting indicator is unique, considering it takes a long time to influence laws, policies and strategies used at the national level. This will be a 5-year target. The achievement of laws and policies will be counted only once.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="3">
      <location ref="Africa"></location>
      <dimension name="Gender" value="Female"></dimension>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In addressing the continuous shrinking policy environment, this year&apos;s work with partners in East Africa resulted in one position paper on Uganda&apos;s Anti-Homosexuality Act (AHA) 2023 and what it meant to the transgender community being released, highlighting critical gaps in understanding and addressing key issues for transgender men and masculine presenting binary folks. Furthermore, a comprehensive review of one Sexual and Gender-Based Violence (SGBV) policy was undertaken with the sector working group in Kenya, highlighting key areas for amendment. For the penal code that criminalizes sex work in Kenya, 20 legislators were convened, proposed and successfully repealed three sections of the penal code, marking progress towards a more just and equitable legal framework for structurally excluded groups.A position paper released on AHA 2023 identifying gaps (Africa row 3)1 SGBV policy reviewed with sector working group and key areas for amendment identified Three sections of the penal code were repealed as proposed by 20 legislators</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
